# account.balance += amount on a field that holds a whole number in 64 bits: a 64-bit addition, and one test that the sum is still a whole number a double can hold. That test stays: nothing bounds the field.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="deposit" role=Source
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[balance]] = Load(b@[[account]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[sum]] = Add({{*}}:Add)
# CHECK: Branch(b@{{*}}, Terminal, {{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:{{*}}Rare:#{{*}}
# CHECK: Store(b@[[sum]], b@[[account]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:PutSlot)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# X64: instructions: 10, patchpoints: 0
# ARM64: instructions: 12, patchpoints: 0
